# E0.2 restart survival, run 1 of 2. Sets 125% on one node and exits.
#
# The scenario DSL cannot restart the app inside one script, so survival is
# two runs against the SAME `TURNSTONE_ROOT`: this one asks for 125% (the
# request lands in the `web.page_scale` facet through the ordinary
# `Effect::SaveSession`), and `browser_zoom_restart_verify.scn` reads it back
# on the restored node without touching the zoom rows.
#
# Start scenarios/fixtures/browser_zoom_server.ps1 on port 43117 first. Run 1
# needs a FRESH profile; run 2 must reuse it.
settle 30
key escape
open http://127.0.0.1:43117/zoom
settle 80
act Toggle live content
settle 80
assert content-live
assert snap page-zoom-requested == 100

act Zoom in
settle 10
act Zoom in
settle 40
assert snap page-zoom-requested == 125
assert snap page-zoom-applied == 125

# The zoom arm already emits SaveSession; this makes the persisted state the
# receipt depends on explicit rather than incidental.
act Save session
settle 40
capture 01_restart_run1_at_125
log E0.2 restart run 1: 125% requested, session saved
